  "description": "The connect ceremony (PROTOCOL 20) with the group bit of ADR 0020: message 3 seals \"grp\":1 beside the inviter's code and name — the invite also brings the acceptor into a group, and nothing says which — and message 4 repeats it. A client that knows the member writes it in every reveal, 0 or 1, so the length of a frame never depends on it; one that does not neither writes nor reads it. The commitments do not cover it (they are computed exactly as in connect.json): it is protected by the AEAD under the channel key. go_ahead is the tag the acceptor's go-ahead (gjoin) carries: HKDF-SHA256 with the channel key as input, a salt of 32 zero bytes and the label as info, 16 bytes, so a go-ahead answers this ceremony and no other. Everything not recorded here is computed as connect.json shows.",
